# Optional overrides — the app ships with working defaults baked in.
# You only need this file if you want to point at a different Dropbox app or folder.
# Copy to .env and set whichever values you want to override.

# ── Dropbox OAuth App Key ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default: 2nrt3uf9qy4oosn (the NAPA Courier Admin Dropbox app)
# Override only if you created your own Dropbox app.
# This is a PKCE client ID — not a secret. Safe to embed in a public client
# per Dropbox's own PKCE documentation; no app secret is used or needed.
#
# To create your own app:
# 1. Go to https://www.dropbox.com/developers/apps
# 2. Click "Create app" → "Scoped access" → "Full Dropbox"
# 3. Under "OAuth 2 → Redirect URIs", add: http://localhost:47291/callback
#    (add 47292–47299 as fallbacks in case that port is in use)
# 4. Under "Permissions", enable: files.content.read, files.content.write, account_info.read
# 5. Copy the "App key" (NOT the App secret — PKCE flow doesn't use it)

# DROPBOX_APP_KEY=your_app_key_here

# ── Default Dropbox folder path ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default: /Delivery Optimization/Delivery Walk Through Videos
# Override only if your shared folder is in a different location.
# Must be an absolute Dropbox path starting with /.
# All five admins must point to the SAME shared folder.
# This can also be changed per-machine in Settings after first run.

# DROPBOX_FOLDER_PATH=/Delivery Optimization/Delivery Walk Through Videos
